```mdl
test T-Create-Filter-And-Pick: typing into the create-object dialog narrows the type list; click commits
  given: I have opened the create-object dialog ("+") in a space
    that has the Bramble plugin enabled
  when: I type a substring of a type name (e.g. "bra" for Bramble)
    into the type search input
  then:
    - the rendered option list narrows to entries whose label
      fuzzy-matches the typed substring; the cursor
      (aria-selected) lands on the highest-scored entry so that
      pressing Enter would commit it
    - the typed substring persists across parent re-renders —
      the filter remains in effect for the duration of the
      user's typing session
    - clicking a remaining entry commits the selection and
      creates an instance of that type; the dialog closes and
      the new object opens in the pane
    - hovering with the mouse highlights the hovered item with
      a clearly visible selection state
  desc: |
    Reported 2026-05-13 as: "the selection of menu items is not
    working — i can't select Bramble and what I do select isn't
    clear". Diagnosis split: the "can't select" half traced to a
    different setup (port 5173 / a separate composer-app
    instance, not this worktree) and is out of scope here.
    What's reproducible against THIS worktree's preview build is
    a narrower pair of upstream defects:

    1. Filter is inert. Typing into the type-search input does
       not narrow the option list — every registered ECHO type
       remains visible and the cursor stays on whichever entry
       auto-selected first (alphabetically, typically "Agent").
       Targeted selection of Bramble (or any other entry) is
       possible by scrolling and clicking; the filter is a
       UX-affordance regression, not a blocker.

       Root cause: `useSearchListResults` in
       @dxos/react-ui-search auto-resets its internal query
       state whenever the `items` prop arrives with a fresh
       array identity. `CreateObjectDialog` rebuilds `options`
       each render (its deps include `manager.capabilities`
       lookups and a `viewTypenames` Set that recomputes on
       schema-registry runs), so any parent re-render between
       the keystroke and the 200 ms `onSearch` debounce wipes
       the user's query.

    2. Mouse hover does not visibly highlight items. The
       `Picker.Item` ships a low-contrast `:hover` background
       (a 97%-light grey on a near-white dialog body) AND keeps
       the keyboard cursor (`aria-selected`, ~89% grey)
       decoupled from the mouse cursor — so users see neither
       a prominent hover-highlight nor a single moving cursor
       that tracks the mouse.

    Both root causes live UPSTREAM of plugin-bramble —
    `useSearchListResults` (in @dxos/react-ui-search) for (1)
    and `Picker.Item` (in @dxos/react-ui-list) for (2). They
    affect every consumer of those primitives, not Bramble
    specifically. Fixes are deliberately OUT OF SCOPE for this
    plugin and are flagged in `## Remaining` for a future
    upstream coordination.

    Captured here so the Bramble create-flow UX expectations
    are documented end-to-end; the test will pass once the
    upstream fixes land.
```

```mdl
test T-PDF-Upload-creates-node: dropping a PDF onto a page creates a new Node carrying the file
  given: a Bramble page open on a pane; plugin-wnfs contributes
    `AppCapabilities.FileUploader`; the user has a local PDF
    file F (e.g. ~100 KB) ready to drag from the OS
  when: I drag F onto the article surface and release the
    pointer over an empty area of the page
  then:
    - a new Bramble.Node N is created with `attachment: {
      kind: 'file', url: <wnfs://… URL>, name: F.name, mimeType:
      'application/pdf', sha256: <SHA-256 hex of F's bytes> }`.
      `Node.kind` is NOT set (it remains undefined per
      F-PDF-Upload.drop-creates-node).
    - N appears in the page as a fresh bullet under the drop-
      site parent (the page node when the drop did not land on
      a specific bullet), wired in via `createEdge` per F-DAG.
    - N's rendered row shows the PDF chip
      (`ph--file-pdf--regular` icon + filename) per
      F-PDF-Upload.chip-rendering.
```

```mdl
test T-PDF-Upload-dedupes-on-second-drop: dropping the SAME PDF a second time reuses the existing Node
  given: a Bramble.Node M already exists in the space with
    `attachment.sha256` equal to the hash of file F (e.g. via
    T-PDF-Upload-creates-node having just run)
  when: I drop F onto a Bramble page a second time
  then:
    - the total count of Bramble.Nodes carrying any
      `attachment.sha256` equal to F's hash remains exactly 1
      (M is reused; no second Node is created).
    - the drop-site parent at the moment of the second drop
      has a structural successor edge pointing at M (added
      via `createEdge` if not already present). The same M is
      now visible at the new drop point AND at its original
      location; the F-DAG multi-parent badge surfaces on every
      occurrence of M (per F-DAG.Phase3e).
```

```mdl
test T-PDF-Upload-chip-opens-file: clicking the PDF chip opens the file in a new tab
  given: a Bramble bullet rendering a Node whose
    `attachment.kind === 'file'` and whose mime type is
    `application/pdf`
  when: I click the PDF chip adjacent to the bullet's content
